    "notes": "Jupiter Island is a barrier island on Florida's Treasure Coast, bounded by the Atlantic Ocean, St. Lucie Inlet, the Indian River, and Jupiter Inlet. The Town of Jupiter Island (Martin County portion, ZIP 33455, area code 772) is described as exceptionally wealthy; Worth magazine (June 1999) ranked it #1 in the U.S. for highest median home sale. Population was 804 at the 2020 census. The island is bordered to the north by the Hobe Sound National Wildlife Refuge; other communities on the island include Jupiter Inlet Colony and the Village of Tequesta. No gate, HOA, or community-amenity information appears in the source content."
